-**Parameters:**
-*   **Step Size ($\Delta t$):** Typically set to half a voxel or 70% of the voxel distance to balance quality and performance [S9][S19].
-*   **Threshold:** Early termination threshold, typically 0.95 or 1.0 [S1, unofficial][S9].
-*   **Sampling Rate ($s$):** Inversely proportional to the distance between samples; it greatly influences the accuracy of approximation and the quality of rendering [S22].
+### Parameters
+*   **Step Size ($\Delta t$)**: Typically set to half a voxel or 70% of the distance between adjacent voxels to satisfy sampling theory and reduce aliasing [S12][S26, unofficial].
+*   **Interpolation Scheme**: Trilinear interpolation is the standard due to hardware support [S5, unofficial].
+*   **Transfer Function**: Maps scalar values to color and opacity. Can be 1D (value-based) or 2D (value and gradient-based) [S7, unofficial][S23, unofficial].
 
-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Aliasing:** Fixed sampling rates cause aliasing artifacts. Mitigated by ray jittering (random offset $t_o \sim U(0, \Delta t)$) [S12].
-*   **Opacity Scaling:** When using lower sampling rates (fewer slices), opacity must be scaled up to maintain overall intensity [S9].
-*   **Undersampling:** Artifacts occur if the convolution of the transfer function and data is undersampled [S18, unofficial].
-*   **Non-Orthogonal Grids:** May require data preparation or correction before rendering [S19].
+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+*   **Aliasing**: Fixed sampling rates can cause "onion ring" artifacts. Mitigated by ray jittering (random offset) or adaptive sampling [S5, unofficial].
+*   **Opacity Scaling**: When using fewer samples (larger step size), opacity must be scaled up to maintain correct visual intensity [S12].
+*   **Boundary Conditions**: Rays may exit the volume before reaching `max_samples`. Entry and exit points should be calculated to limit the marching range [S12].
+*   **Gradient Dependence**: Gradient estimation for shading should be independent of the classification scheme to avoid artifacts [S11, unofficial].
 
